      faq: [['Why is inlining so important?', 'It removes calls and enables other optimisations across method boundaries.'], ['Default size limit for non-hot inlining?', '35 bytes of bytecode.'], ['What is a megamorphic call site?', 'One that has seen many receiver types.'], ['What does scalar replacement do?', 'Replaces a non-escaping object with local variables.'], ['What is lock elision?', 'Removing locks on objects no other thread can see.']],
