        explain: "Container failures without a Java `OutOfMemoryError` usually mean total process memory exceeded the limit: heap plus non-heap. Budget explicitly: heap, Metaspace (often 100–300 MB for frameworks), thread stacks (platform threads × stack size), code cache (up to 240 MB by default with tiered compilation), direct buffers (Netty), and native libraries. CPU limits below one core make GC and JIT threads compete with application threads; very small CPU quotas cause throttling that looks like random latency spikes. For profiling, prefer sampling profilers in production; instrumentation profilers distort timings. Read flame graphs top-down from the widest frames, and compare before/after recordings for regressions. Treat heap dumps and JFR files as sensitive data: they can contain passwords, tokens, and personal data held in memory.",
